OTools Ziplark Plugin
=====================

This repository is a port of Ziplark (https://github.com/zhitongblog/ziplark),
MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 doaipm. The upstream snapshot was taken at
commit 9d539b6 ("fix: prompt for password on data-encrypted RAR/ZIP/7z
archives") and is preserved verbatim under upstream/.

What was ported
---------------
* upstream/ui/                     the vanilla HTML/CSS/JS desktop frontend,
                                   used without a single source modification.
* upstream/ziplark-core/           the Rust archive engine, used unmodified as
                                   the source of native/ziplark-core/.
* upstream/tauri-commands.reference.rs
                                   the upstream Tauri command layer, kept only
                                   as a behavioural reference for native/src/.

What is new in this repository
------------------------------
* native/                          OTools cdylib plugin backend. Exposes
                                   otools_plugin_invoke / otools_plugin_free
                                   and the optional poll_events channel.
* shell/                           the OTools host bridge (native invoke,
                                   SDK file picker, drag & drop, open-file).
* scripts/, .github/workflows/     build, packaging and release tooling.

Third-party components keep their own licenses. In particular RAR extraction
uses the UnRAR library, which is NOT MIT licensed and may not be used to
re-create the RAR compression algorithm. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

The OTools host SDK (vendor/otools-plugin-sdk-dist/) and the FFI helper
(vendor/ot-plugin-ffi/) come from the OTools project and retain their own
licenses.

